# Use `100dvh` not `100vh`

Always use `100dvh` (dynamic viewport height) instead of `100vh` for any element intended to fill the screen height — backgrounds, modals, overlays, fixed backdrops.

`100vh` on iOS Safari is calculated from the full viewport including hidden browser chrome, so it does not shrink when the keyboard opens, leaving a white gap below the content.

```tsx
/* ✅ correct */
style={{ minHeight: "100dvh" }}
style={{ height: "100dvh" }}

/* ❌ never */
style={{ minHeight: "100vh" }}
style={{ height: "100vh" }}
```

This applies to all components: page wrappers, `position: fixed` backdrops, modals, sheets, and overlays.
